  "name": "Objective the sampled rate cannot move",
  "description": "R is fed by twelve transitions (f0..f11) whose rates are never sampled; B by tA, which is. Every sample therefore has the same R, an exact tie, so the Pareto front (max R, max B) is the one sample with the largest B. A solver whose flux sums vary between calls breaks the tie at random.",
